  "body": "Original read/resolve routes match, but retained traces do not contain returned pixel buffers. This adds a bounded C return-buffer core and strict Python codec/candidate matcher, verified only with compiled CPU fake originals. It installs no live adapter and observes no new GPU bytes. Original strict0/4FAIL and Stage7INCOMPLETE remain.\n\nThe core forwards original arguments once, snapshots supplied pre-call metadata, copies after return, preserves errno, and rejects unsupported/PBO/short/overlapping/aliased buffers. OFF does not inspect metadata or pixels. Window/global limits, owner-thread/reentrancy and sticky failures bound observation while originals keep running. The160Bheader/96Bfooter stream normalizes RGB/RGBA/BGR/BGRA to top-down RGB. Completion additionally requires trusted out-of-band post-finish status/counters bound to nonce and finalized stream SHA/length. A complete footer cannot attest its own emitter result. Unique byte candidates convey no native/GPU-write/physical-frame authority.\n\nStatic pinned wheel/source/ELF metadata matches installed identities and identifies the original read import and outer method relocations. It proves no compiled instruction ABI or real Texture span. The existing sealed environment rejects added preload and is unchanged. Actual dispatch/span/pack/context/camera/receipt transport and a new runtime contract/fresh bounded canary remain inactive qualification gates. No old consumed request is reapplied.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 29focused tests PASS; whole suite1351tests PASS,7skip,121.931s.\n- 25compiled synthetic scenarios pass ASan/UBSan with identical streams/stats; max24records55,900,512B within64MiBwire/8MiBsource-span limits.\n- One fresh whole-branch source+synthetic-data review: Critical0,Important2,Minor0. One TDD fix pass corrects excess-window capture and full-footer/emitter-failure acceptance. No rereview.\n- 71indexed proofs13,023,869B, including reviewed pre-fix copies and active receipts; all source/binary/raw identities verified. Final synthetic build smoke3.795422940s wall excludes tests/review/CI/development and is no GL-overhead measurement.\n- All2431base tracked files and299old source pins preserved; original2traces/4graphs/4sealed ZIPs match. Main, old Draft102/103/104 and eight native workflow histories unchanged. New native/GL/provider/officialmodel/officialORT counts0; consumed native allowance remaining0.\n\nRulings I made (exhaustive; costs if wrong):\n\n1. Continue inline in the current checkout/own branch under persistent user authorization, without repeated questions or another worktree; spends development/CPU effort and no native allowance.\n2. Build an injectable CPU core rather than load an interposer; static call points lack qualified extent/identity/environment suppliers, so real-byte observation remains deferred.\n3. Preserve original calls/errno even when observation fails; failures invalidate capture acceptance while application calls continue.\n4. Treat after-call memory and supplied labels as candidates; void return/equal bytes do not prove GPU success/freshness/physical frame, so causal qualification remains future work.\n5. Correct independent fixture tuple indices22..25 to match hand-counted160Bwire; leaving them wrong would misparse every record.\n6. Keep actual adapter/runtime admission inactive; CPUmalloc and static ELF/source tests do not qualify dispatch/span/camera, requiring a new mechanical contract and bounded canary.\n7. Require external producer-finalization receipt; footer cannot attest its own emission result. Consumers must supply actual post-finish stats and finalized spool identity, and qualify transport before native use. An invented receipt conveys no native authority.\n8. Review set-aside dispatch/instruction binding remains unproven; live adapter qualification is still required.\n9. Review set-aside Texture/view extent and camera identity remain caller preconditions; bad future suppliers could read wrong memory or mislabel candidates until qualified.\n10. Review set-aside GPU success/freshness/physical frame remain unproven; real correspondence evidence is still needed.\n11. Review set-aside live concurrency/overhead remain unmeasured; serialized fake+sanitizers cannot establish native races/scheduling/performance, so bounded controls/thread qualification remain required.\n12. Review set-aside valid context/storage/metadata lifetime, serialized lifecycle and normally returning original remain C API preconditions; violations can fault and are outside accepted integration.\n13. Review set-aside runtime admission/fresh allowance/deployment remain inactive; old sealed contract rejects preload and a new contract/canary review is required.\n\nDeferred minors: none.\n\nResult: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_RETURN_CORE_RESULT.md\nLedger: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_RETURN_CORE_LEDGER.md\nProofs: docs/evidence/readback-return-core-01/proof-index.json\nOriginal review: docs/evidence/READBACK_RETURN_CORE_01_REVIEW.md\n\nThis Draft stacks on feature/gl-read-provenance-v1 atf8994f1. No shared base/main push, merge, Cloud/registry publication or native activation. Exact-head CI closeout below is external to the immutable source commit.\n\nExact-head closeout (2026-11-14T23:39:14.094168+09:00):\n\nSourcea0e072e450cf6591b9da686711196d56eb9165a1; Draft105 remains unmerged; basef8994f1; body roundtrip verified.\n\n- pull_request: https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43605849109 \u2014 success,attempt1,2jobs,0artifacts; jobIDs 132480193738,132480193909.\n- push: https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43605824432 \u2014 success,attempt1,2jobs,0artifacts; jobIDs 132480119256,132480119794.\n\nFinal recheck: all2431base tracked files/299sourcepins/10original artifacts match;71proofs13,023,869B are in Git;84added paths and0base/workflow edits; main48e79a7ed5aedf6daa5a62ff68d2225af7955ef1/oldDrafts/nativehistories unchanged. No new native/GL/provider/officialmodel/officialORT; consumed allowance0remaining. Actual GPU bytes/runtime/receipt transport remain unqualified. Final closeout retained at output/stage7-readback-return-core/final-verification.json.\n",
